<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Socialist Party of Albania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1991">1991</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Socialist Party of Albania is a centre-left party founded in 1991 as the successor of the communist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/party-of-labour-of-albania">Party of Labour of Albania</a>. It governed from 1997 to 2005 and has held power again since 2013 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edi-rama">Edi Rama</a>. Its rivalry with the Democratic Party has shaped Albanian politics since the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communism">communism</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/party-of-labour-of-albania">Party of Labour of Albania</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enver-hoxha">Enver Hoxha</a>, had ruled the country for over four decades. Hoxha's successor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramiz-alia">Ramiz Alia</a>, was forced to introduce limited reforms in the late 1980s, and on 11 December 1990 he announced that the party had given up its monopoly of power. It won the Constitutional Assembly election of 1991, the first free elections held in Albania in almost 80 years, by which time it was no longer a Marxist-Leninist party. At an extraordinary congress held from 10 to 13 June 1991 it reorganised itself as the Socialist Party in order to survive in the new system.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">History</h2><p>Fatos Nano, a man from the intelligentsia, was elected the first chairman. He helped to reform the old communist party and brought it into the Socialist International. In 2004 a faction led by Ilir Meta broke away and formed the Socialist Movement for Integration. On 10 October 2005, after losing the parliamentary election of that year, Nano resigned and was succeeded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edi-rama">Edi Rama</a>.</p><p>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama">Rama</a> the party formed the Alliance for a European Albania, which united several parties and won the parliamentary election of 2013, returning the Socialists to government after eight years. Running alone, the party won the elections of 2017 and 2021 with 74 seats in each, enough to govern by itself, though it has had the outside support of the Social Democratic Party in parliament.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Organisation and way of life</h2><p>The party is described as social-democratic. Its platform of 2013 pledged to replace the flat tax with a progressive tax and supported universal health care. It is pro-European, supports Albania's accession to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a> and its membership of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a>, and regards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a> as the country's main strategic partner and ally. It is an associate of the Party of European Socialists. Its emblem is based on the fist and rose designed by José María Cruz Novillo for the Spanish Socialist Workers' Party in 1977, used without that party's official consent.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Socialist Party of Albania” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
